"""
backbone_distill.py — depth-pruned PersonaPlex backbone distillation
====================================================================

Implements `backbone_distillation_demo_plan.md`.  This is a *different* track
from the grouped DepFormer work: the backbone (main temporal transformer) is
made smaller by keeping a subset of the teacher's layers, keeping `d_model`,
the embeddings, `out_norm`, `text_linear`, Mimi and the DepFormer unchanged.

Pieces in this file (first slice)
--------------------------------
* :func:`select_layers` / :func:`block_influence` — choose which teacher layers
  to keep (spaced or contiguous, always keep the first/last few).
* :func:`build_student` — construct an `LMModel` with `len(kept)` layers and
  initialise every shared tensor from the teacher, with student layer `i` taking
  teacher layer `kept[i]` (no random init).
* :func:`forward_distill` — one teacher-forced pass returning post-`out_norm`
  hidden states, undelayed text logits, undelayed DepFormer audio logits and
  optional intermediate layer features.  Used for both the frozen teacher
  (`no_grad`) and the student (with grad).
* Losses: `L_h` (per-dim-normalised MSE + cosine), `L_text` (full KL + top-k /
  temperature-matched KL, non-PAD up-weighted), `L_audio` (frozen-DepFormer KL on
  agent slots), optional `L_feat` (mapped intermediate layers, stage 1).
* `_self_test` — CPU end-to-end including the plan's S0 sanity: a student with
  **0 layers dropped** must equal the teacher.

Still to come (tracked by the plan): batched rollout token generation (§3.3),
layer-drop ablation runner (§4.1), the multi-stage trainer with fp32 master
weights + 8-bit AdamW, on-policy round (§5.4), PTQ for the depformer hand-off.
"""

